<title>SWEDEN: Nov Norscan pulp seen up 185,000 tonnes - Sodra.</title>
<headline>Nov Norscan pulp seen up 185,000 tonnes - Sodra.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>North American/Scandinavian Norscan pulp inventories rose by 185,000 tonnes in November according to preliminary figures, a spokesman from Swedish pulp producer Sodra Skogsagarna said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;In the U.S. and Canada stocks increased by 155,000 tonnes and in Scandinavia by 30,000 tonnes,&quot; Hans Burmeister, head of Sodra's marketing division, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;These are still preliminary figures and I believe the definitive figures will be published this afternoon or tomorrow,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Jorgen Osterberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1008</p>
</text>
